      "end": 2.88,
      "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.93,
      "end": 17.41,
      "text": "You can. You'll want a small long handled pot, very finely ground coffee, almost like powder, and cold water."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.82,
      "end": 26.96,
      "text": "Many shops sell coffee ground specifically for it. Regular coffee ground on the finest setting can work if your grinder goes that fine."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 34.23,
      "end": 41.14,
      "text": "That's because the sugar goes in at the start. You mix coffee, sugar and water in the pot, then heat it slowly without boiling."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 44.07,
      "end": 52.25,
      "text": "When a thick foam rises up to the top, take it off the heat just before it boils over. Pour gently to keep the foam, and let the grounds settle before sipping."
